; Manifest-phase family, 2 of 6 — the other advisory one. `Plugin.MAX_KEYWORDS`
; is 16 and this declares 17.
;
; "Advisory cap" means the list is not truncated and the plugin is not
; rejected: all 17 keywords are kept and `(pt :x 1)` validates. A cap that
; only warns is easy to turn into a cap that silently truncates, or into an
; error, by someone reading the constant alone — this case pins which of the
; three it is.
(plugin :name probe :version "1.0.0"
  :keywords [k1 k2 k3 k4 k5 k6 k7 k8 k9 k10 k11 k12 k13 k14 k15 k16 k17]
  (form :name pt (key :name x :type number)))

(pt :x 1)
